// Load buffering with a dependency on both sides, under sMRD.
//
// MRD's headline no-thin-air result: the write of y is reached only when r1 is
// positive and writes r1's own value, so it depends on the read of x, and
// symmetrically on the other side. The outcome needs each read to be justified
// by a cycle through its own dependency, which is thin air.
//
// pldi_repairing/LB+deps.lit is the same program asked of RC11, which forbids
// it for a blunter reason -- acyclic(sb u rf) forbids every load-buffering
// shape, dependency or not (see pldi_repairing/LB.lit). This file is the one
// that exercises sMRD's own dependency reasoning, and it is what MRD exists to
// deliver.
//
// It was allowed until ValueAssignElab stopped discharging the conjuncts that
// pin a write's own value: a model of `r1 > 0` concretised `W y r1` to `W y 1`
// and dropped `r1 > 0` in the same step, so the write depended on nothing.
// 5 executions became 1. The constant-valued variant next door was forbidden
// throughout, which is what made the mechanism visible.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  r1 := x;
  if (r1 > 0) {
    y := r1
  }
} ||| {
  r2 := y;
  if (r2 > 0) {
    x := r2
  }
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1) []
